────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. ACCEPTABLE USE

The Software MUST NOT be used to:

  (a) Obtain an undisclosed advantage in any examination, certification,
      interview, take-home assignment, live coding test, technical
      assessment, academic submission, or other evaluative process where
      use of AI assistance is not openly disclosed to, and explicitly
      permitted by, all relevant evaluators or counterparties.

  (b) Deceive any employer, recruiter, educator, examiner, client,
      audience, or counterparty about the source, authorship, or
      provenance of one's work, knowledge, capabilities, or
      qualifications.

  (c) Circumvent, defeat, or evade monitoring, proctoring, screen-sharing,
      or integrity-enforcement tools used by an institution, employer,
      platform, or examiner — including, but not limited to, the use of
      this Software's screen-capture-invisible overlay feature during
      sessions where its presence has not been disclosed.

  (d) Violate any applicable academic-integrity policy, employment
      agreement, code of conduct, or terms of service of any platform on
      which the Software is operated or with which it interacts.

  (e) Engage in activity prohibited by Anthropic's Usage Policies
      (https://www.anthropic.com/legal/aup), the terms of any LLM
      provider invoked by the Software, or any applicable law.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. PERMITTED USE (non-exhaustive)

Permitted uses include, but are not limited to:

  • Personal productivity and learning on one's own machine.
  • Speaker notes / teleprompter use during livestreams or recordings
    that one personally controls.
  • Research, debugging, and reading assistance for one's own materials.
  • Accessibility aids.
  • Any other use that respects Section 1.

